      "type": "teach",
      "title": "The other half of the pair",
      "body": "These two are not new arrivals so much as the partners of the letters you just learned: 𐑮 belongs with 𐑤, and 𐑯 belongs with 𐑥 — one tall, one deep, the same shape either way up. That is why they arrive together, and it is also the reason people mix up l with r and m with n. Meet them side by side and the confusion never starts.",
